                <fr:title text="questions from the pre-readings">questions from the pre-readings</fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:ul>
                  <html:li>
            One of the suggested pre-readings is <fr:link href="/forest/grayson-2018/" title="An introduction to univalent foundations for mathematicians" uri="http://localhost:4000/forest/grayson-2018/" display-uri="grayson-2018" type="local">An introduction to univalent foundations for mathematicians</fr:link>.
            On p.20, the so-called "'resizing' rules" are mentioned and the
            consistency of such a system is left open.
            Apparently, this is still open as of
            <fr:link href="https://benediktahrens.gitlab.io/talks/HTT-UF-Leeds2019.pdf" type="external">2019</fr:link>.
            Is this still open today? Is anyone working on it? Does anyone
            still care? Or are people complacent with universe polymorphism and
            just lifting everything?
        </html:li>
                </html:ul>
